"fill:none" d="M 152.08 -87.23 L 112.59 -87.23"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 112.59 -87.23)"><path d="M 5.26 0 C 4.61 0.16 1.77 1.04 0 2.01 L 0 -2.01 C 1.77 -1.04 4.61 -0.16 5.26 0 Z"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 106.91 -71.97 L -99.22 -71.97 C -100.75 -71.97 -101.98 -73.21 -101.98 -74.74 L -101.98 -99.71 C -101.98 -101.24 -100.75 -102.48 -99.22 -102.48 L 106.91 -102.48 C 108.44 -102.48 109.68 -101.24 109.68 -99.71 L 109.68 -74.74 C 109.68 -73.21 108.44 -71.97 106.91 -71.97 Z M -101.98 -102.48"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -97.83 -87.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:18.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="0" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)" width="255.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.12" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:18.44em;">
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.12.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -71.17 -64.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:16.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:6.81pt;" height="6.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.19)" width="151.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F1.pic1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">Lean 4 (machine-checked semantics)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic gap: the standard pipeline (top) chains PyTorch <math id="S1.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> Export <math id="S1.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> ONNX <math id="S1.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> Verifier, with potential drift at each conversion step; <span id="S1.F1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TorchLean</span> (bottom) keeps a single shared IR as the semantic target for both execution and verification (Verifier artifacts are checked against this same meaning).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Neural networks are increasingly embedded in systems where mistakes have physical or societal cost, and the machine learning community is correspondingly placing more weight on guarantees that go beyond empirical accuracy: robustness to perturbations, satisfaction of hard safety/stability constraints, and conservative bounds on quantities derived from a network’s computation. This has driven an active verification ecosystem spanning <em id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">solver-based</em> approaches that reduce verification queries to constraint solving (e.g., SMT/MILP-style tools such as Reluplex and Marabou for piecewise-linear networks) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Katz et al., 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Katz et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, as well as <em id="S1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">scalable</em> relaxation and abstract interpretation based methods that compute certified enclosures via bound propagation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gowal et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Singh et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Surveys and systems papers emphasize that such techniques are now core to validating learning-enabled components in safety-critical autonomy and control pipelines <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiang et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. Despite this progress, turning verifier outputs into dependable end-to-end guarantees remains challenging in practice; to motivate our approach, we next highlight three concrete <span id="S1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">failure modes</span>:</p>
</div>
