<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VNN-COMP-style suites (ONNX + VNNLIB).</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the VNN-COMP convention that each benchmark instance is an ONNX network paired with a VNN-LIB property specification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">VNN-COMP, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">VNN-LIB, 2021</a>)</cite>. A lightweight Python export step converts ONNX/VNN-LIB into compact JSON bundles consumed by a Lean runner, which checks a <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sufficient UNSAT</em> condition by replaying IBP/CROWN-style bounds against the shared IR semantics (fast runtime <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Float</span>). Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3 Results ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports results on small MNIST-FC and ACASXu slices: IBP is conservative, while objective-dependent CROWN refutes some MNIST-FC properties; importing optimized <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> slopes mainly improves runtime. Details of the interface and schemas are in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 VNN-COMP / VNN-LIB interface (ONNX + VNNLIB) ‣ Appendix D CROWN verification: bounds, duality, and certificates ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S3.F5.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:339.6pt;height:184.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="S3.F5.3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="255.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 469.9 255.75" width="469.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,255.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(234.96,0) translate(0,219.15)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 229.14 36.32 L -229.14 36.32 C -232.2 36.32 -234.68 33.84 -234.68 30.79 L -234.68 -30.79 C -234.68 -33.84 -232.2 -36.32 -229.14 -36.32 L 229.14 -36.32 C 232.2 -36.32 234.68 -33.84 234.68 -30.79 L 234.68 30.79 C 234.68 33.84 232.2 36.32 229.14 36.32 Z M -234.68 -36.32"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -229.14 22.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.96em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.85em;font-size:10pt;" height="61.58" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="539.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:38.96em;">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">UAT (classical).
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-1.7pt;"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For any continuous <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on a compact domain (e.g., <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a
single-hidden-layer ReLU MLP <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x\in[-1,1]^{d}}|N(x)-f(x)|\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x\in[-1,1]^{d}}|N(x)-f(x)|\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#666666;">App. <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Universal Approximation Theorems ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7F7;" fill="#F7F7F7"><path d="M 229.14 36.32 L 219 36.32 C 215.94 36.32 213.46 33.84 213.46 30.79 L 213.46 31.81 C 213.46 28.75 215.94 26.27 219 26.27 L 229.14 26.27 C 232.2 26.27 234.68 28.75 234.68 31.81 L 234.68 30.79 C 234.68 33.84 232.2 36.32 229.14 36.32 Z M 213.46 26.27"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 215.12 27.94)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="6.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="17.89"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">real</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 229.14 -48.69 L -229.14 -48.69 C -232.2 -48.69 -234.68 -51.16 -234.68 -54.22 L -234.68 -149 C -234.68 -152.06 -232.2 -154.54 -229.14 -154.54 L 229.14 -154.54 C 232.2 -154.54 234.68 -152.06 234.68 -149 L 234.68 -54.22 C 234.68 -51.16 232.2 -48.69 229.14 -48.69 Z M -234.68 -154.54"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -229.14 -62.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.96em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="94.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="539.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:38.96em;">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.3.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.3.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Toward IUA (Float32-exec).
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-1.7pt;"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For a fixed network <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and input box <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, we mechanize an interval evaluator <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\sharp}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\sharp}(B)</annotation></semantics></math> and
prove a sound enclosure: all <span id="S3.F5.pic1.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IEEE32Exec</span> executions <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(x)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(N^{\sharp}(B))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(N^{\sharp}(B))</annotation></semantics></math>
(soundness; not yet the exact hull).
 <span id="S3.F5.pic1.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#666666;">App. <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Float32-exec Soundness ‣ Appendix E Universal Approximation Theorems ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7F7;" fill="#F7F7F7"><path d="M 229.14 -48.69 L 176.46 -48.69 C 173.4 -48.69 170.92 -51.16 170.92 -54.22 L 170.92 -53.09 C 170.92 -56.15 173.4 -58.63 176.46 -58.63 L 229.14 -58.63 C 232.2 -58.63 234.68 -56.15 234.68 -53.09 L 234.68 -54.22 C 234.68 -51.16 232.2 -48.69 229.14 -48.69 Z M 170.92 -58.63"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 172.58 -56.97)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.48em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="6.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="60.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">IEEE32Exec</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 229.14 -166.9 L -229.14 -166.9 C -232.2 -166.9 -234.68 -169.38 -234.68 -172.44 L -234.68 -213.33 C -234.68 -216.39 -232.2 -218.87 -229.14 -218.87 L 229.14 -218.87 C 232.2 -218.87 234.68 -216.39 234.68 -213.33 L 234.68 -172.44 C 234.68 -169.38 232.2 -166.9 229.14 -166.9 Z M -234.68 -218.87"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -229.14 -180.13)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.96em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.4em;font-size:10pt;" height="40.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="539.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:38.96em;">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.5.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.5.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Same artifact.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-1.7pt;"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
One Lean model definition <math id="S3.F5.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> executable training + compiled SSA/DAG IR reused for verification.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S3.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Theory + execution: UAT and IEEE32Exec soundness.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case studies: Certified Robustness, PINN residual bounds, and a Neural controller.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Certified Robustness.</span>
We certify an <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> margin condition for a digits linear classifier (<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sklearn</span> digits, 8<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>8<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>64 features; 64<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>10; <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>). As summarized in Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ VNN-COMP-style suites (ONNX + VNNLIB). ‣ 3 Results ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the model is nominally correct on <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="349/360" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>349</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>360</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">349/360</annotation></semantics></math> test inputs and <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">certified robust</em> on <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="318/360" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>318</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>360</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">318/360</annotation></semantics></math>. A small Lean checker replays these results directly from the exported bound artifact by verifying the standard logit-margin inequality (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D CROWN verification: bounds, duality, and certificates ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>); checking is lightweight (0.032 ms avg, 0.057 ms max; Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ VNN-COMP-style suites (ONNX + VNNLIB). ‣ 3 Results ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3 Results ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> further reports how IBP certificate runtime and artifact size scale with MLP parameter count.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S3.F6.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:1385.2pt;height:771.9pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="S3.F6.3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2602.22631v1/ibp_scaling.png" id="S3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:1912/1068;" width="1912" height="1068" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="S3.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">IBP scaling on MLPs (in=hid, out=10, 3 layers). Wall time (left axis) and certificate artifact size in bytes (right axis) versus parameter count. Both increase with model size, quantifying checker cost and proof-artifact overhead.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Robustness case study (digits linear classifier).</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Dataset</span></td>
<td id="S3.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">sklearn<span id="S3.T3.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> digits (8<math id="S3.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>8)</span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model</span></td>
<td id="S3.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="S3.T3.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Linear (64<math id="S3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.T3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Norm / radius</span></td>
<td id="S3.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="S3.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T3.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, <math id="S3.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0.02</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T3.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.T3.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Nominally correct</span></td>
