<span id="S3.F7.pic1.15.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.F7.pic1.15.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">External solver
<br class="ltx_break">(<math id="S3.F7.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-CROWN)
<br class="ltx_break">certificates</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.35pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 23.62 -124.91 L 23.62 -124.91 L -40.61 -124.91 L -40.61 -143.89"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -40.61 -143.89)"><path d="M 5.12 0 C 4.49 0.15 1.73 1.01 0 1.95 L 0 -1.95 C 1.73 -1.01 4.49 -0.15 5.12 0 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.22 -196.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:6.81pt;" height="6.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.19)" width="338.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F7.pic1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">TCB minimized to IR semantics + checker (external solvers optional/untrusted).</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="S3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Neural-controller workflow in three execution settings. All pipelines compile to a shared op-tagged SSA/DAG IR and are verified inside Lean; external optimizers act only as untrusted certificate producers.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PINN residual bounds:</span> we demonstrate end-to-end verification of physics-informed neural networks trained to satisfy PDEs. The workflow begins with training a PINN model in Python (e.g., viscous Burgers equation <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}+u\cdot u_{x}-\nu u_{xx}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}+u\cdot u_{x}-\nu u_{xx}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) using PyTorch autograd to compute derivatives for the PDE residual loss. After training, we export weights to JSON and load them into Lean. For verification, we compute bounds on <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x)</annotation></semantics></math> via IBP/CROWN, and compute interval enclosures for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime\prime}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime\prime}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> via dedicated first/second-derivative bound-propagation passes on the same op-tagged graph (covering the smooth ops used in the PINN demos, e.g. <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tanh</span> and linear layers), rather than by recursively differentiating the backward graph. These bounds are then combined to certify that the PDE residual <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{R}(u_{\theta})(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{R}(u_{\theta})(x)|</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded within tolerance <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> at verification points (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D CROWN verification: bounds, duality, and certificates ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T4" class="ltx_table">

