<tr id="A2.T5.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T5.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.1pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Reverse-mode AD</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:158.7pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Backpropagation equals the adjoint Fréchet derivative for well-typed SSA/DAG graphs over </span><math id="A2.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T5.6.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, assuming local per-op derivative correctness (with a pointwise variant for non-smooth ops).</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:48.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Proved</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.1pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Theorem </span><a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 NN.Runtime ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a><span id="A2.T5.6.3.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, Appendix </span><a href="#A2" title="Appendix B TorchLean: a PyTorch-style front end with a single semantic target ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.6.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T5.6.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.1pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:70%;">TorchLean</span><span id="A2.T5.6.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> compilation</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:158.7pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">“Compiled mode” produces the verifier-facing IR; full compiler correctness for arbitrary </span><span id="A2.T5.6.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:70%;">TorchLean</span><span id="A2.T5.6.4.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> programs is not yet proved.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:48.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Proved (fragment) / Future (full)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.1pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Theorem </span><a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Execution modes and compilation to IR ‣ Appendix B TorchLean: a PyTorch-style front end with a single semantic target ‣ TorchLean: Formalizing Neural Networks in Lean" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.6.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T5.6.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:62.1pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">IBP / CROWN operators</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:158.7pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T5.6.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Sound transfer rules and relaxations for a curated set of operators; additional ops use conservative fallbacks or are treated as unsupported in the strongest theorems.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.6.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.6.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:48.3pt;">
