<div id="A2.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 75" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000099;" fill="#000099" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.6 L 0 71.41 C 0 73.39 1.61 75 3.6 75 L 473.78 75 C 475.77 75 477.38 73.39 477.38 71.41 L 477.38 3.6 C 477.38 1.61 475.77 0 473.78 0 L 3.6 0 C 1.61 0 0 1.61 0 3.6 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7F7;" fill="#F7F7F7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.6 L 0.83 53.17 L 476.55 53.17 L 476.55 3.6 C 476.55 2.07 475.31 0.83 473.78 0.83 L 3.6 0.83 C 2.07 0.83 0.83 2.07 0.83 3.6 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000099;" fill="#000099" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 54 L 0.83 71.41 C 0.83 72.93 2.07 74.17 3.6 74.17 L 473.78 74.17 C 475.31 74.17 476.55 72.93 476.55 71.41 L 476.55 54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000099;--ltx-fill-color:#000099;--ltx-fg-color:#000099;" color="#000099" fill="#000099" stroke="#000099" stroke-width="2.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.38 75 L 1.38 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 60.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:28.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="392.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:28.36em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Theorem B.4: </span><span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Tensor–vector inner-product bridge</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 15.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.61em;--ltx-fo-height:1.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.26em;font-size:10pt;" height="30.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.98)" width="451.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.61em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For any shape <math id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and tensors <math id="A2.SS4.p11.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathrm{Tensor}(\mathbb{R},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Tensor</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathrm{Tensor}(\mathbb{R},s)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle a,b\rangle_{s}\;=\;\big\langle\mathrm{vec}_{s}(a),\,\mathrm{vec}_{s}(b)\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{\mathrm{size}(s)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vec</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vec</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">size</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle a,b\rangle_{s}\;=\;\big\langle\mathrm{vec}_{s}(a),\,\mathrm{vec}_{s}(b)\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{\mathrm{size}(s)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">From local calculus to graph calculus.</span>
For each primitive operator (node kind), we prove a standard calculus fact: its forward-mode JVP coincides with applying
its Fréchet derivative to a tangent vector at the current input (and similarly, its VJP coincides with applying the adjoint
of that derivative to a cotangent seed). Combining these node-level facts with the SSA/DAG structure yields a global theorem
for any well-typed graph. In finite dimensions, the adjoint of a linear map is just the transpose with respect to the Euclidean
inner product; operationally, this is exactly what reverse-mode backprop computes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="192.1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 192.1" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,192.1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000099;" fill="#000099" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.6 L 0 188.5 C 0 190.49 1.61 192.1 3.6 192.1 L 473.78 192.1 C 475.77 192.1 477.38 190.49 477.38 188.5 L 477.38 3.6 C 477.38 1.61 475.77 0 473.78 0 L 3.6 0 C 1.61 0 0 1.61 0 3.6 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7F7;" fill="#F7F7F7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.6 L 0.83 170.27 L 476.55 170.27 L 476.55 3.6 C 476.55 2.07 475.31 0.83 473.78 0.83 L 3.6 0.83 C 2.07 0.83 0.83 2.07 0.83 3.6 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000099;" fill="#000099" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 171.1 L 0.83 188.5 C 0.83 190.03 2.07 191.27 3.6 191.27 L 473.78 191.27 C 475.31 191.27 476.55 190.03 476.55 188.5 L 476.55 171.1 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000099;--ltx-fill-color:#000099;--ltx-fg-color:#000099;" color="#000099" fill="#000099" stroke="#000099" stroke-width="2.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.38 192.1 L 1.38 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 177.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:28.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="392.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:28.36em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Theorem B.5: </span><span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Backpropagation computes the adjoint derivative</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 14.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.61em;--ltx-fo-height:10.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="147.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 145.04)" width="451.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.61em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a well-typed SSA/DAG graph over <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{EvalVec}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝖤𝗏𝖺𝗅𝖵𝖾𝖼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{EvalVec}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its vectorized denotation.
Assume the graph satisfies the local differentiability hypotheses for its primitives (i.e., <span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GraphFDerivCorrect</span> <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>).
Then for any input <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and cotangent seed <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{VJP}_{G}(x;\bar{y})\;=\;\bigl(D\,\mathsf{EvalVec}_{G}(x)\bigr)^{\top}\,\bar{y}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝖵𝖩𝖯</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝖤𝗏𝖺𝗅𝖵𝖾𝖼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{VJP}_{G}(x;\bar{y})\;=\;\bigl(D\,\mathsf{EvalVec}_{G}(x)\bigr)^{\top}\,\bar{y},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\,\mathsf{EvalVec}_{G}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝖤𝗏𝖺𝗅𝖵𝖾𝖼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\,\mathsf{EvalVec}_{G}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Fréchet derivative (Jacobian as a linear map) and <math id="A2.SS4.p13.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes its adjoint
(transpose) with respect to the standard inner product.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Interpretation.</em> The theorem states that reverse-mode backprop is not merely an implementation heuristic: it computes
the mathematically correct cotangent propagation associated with the derivative of the graph denotation. For non-smooth or
domain-sensitive primitives (e.g., ReLU at <math id="A2.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math> at nonpositive inputs), we use a pointwise variant with explicit side
conditions that rule out problematic points.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F10" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F10.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="210.25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 457.8 210.25" width="457.8"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,210.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(61.83,0) translate(0,185.12)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 56.01 24.86 L -56.01 24.86 C -59.07 24.86 -61.55 22.38 -61.55 19.32 L -61.55 -19.32 C -61.55 -22.38 -59.07 -24.86 -56.01 -24.86 L 56.01 -24.86 C 59.07 -24.86 61.55 -22.38 61.55 -19.32 L 61.55 19.32 C 61.55 22.38 59.07 24.86 56.01 24.86 Z M -61.55 -24.86"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.92 0.0 0.0 0.92 -57.09 13.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.65em;font-size:10pt;" height="44.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="145.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
